---
/**
 * trades / PageBQ — "Bakal Fabrication Works" (steel fabrication, welding,
 * metal shops).
 *
 * Near-black sheet, bone-white type, one hazard orange-red and a stone band.
 * Oswald condensed uppercase over Source Sans 3. The design's three signatures:
 *
 *   1. THE ANGLED CUT. The hero photo band and the closing band are sheared
 *      with clip-path polygons — a plate cut off-square. Nothing else in the
 *      template is angled, which is what keeps them reading as a cut.
 *   2. THE JOB SHEET. Services are not cards; they are a ruled spec table
 *      (Ref, Job, Material, Finish, Lead time). It is the block a fabricator
 *      actually hands across a counter.
 *   3. THE STONE BANDS. Two full-bleed inversions on #C9C4B8 (the proof strip
 *      and the process band) break the dark sheet into three acts.
 *
 * ROLE OF THIS FILE: the wrapper emits the WHOLE document (doctype, head,
 * tokens, fonts, Leaflet boot, skip link, scroll-reveal). It does NOT compose
 * with BaseLayout. It is the only file in the variant that touches `siteData`;
 * the 15 section components receive only `layout` + `content`.
 *
 * EDITABLE HOOKS OWNED BY THIS FILE: none. PageBQ renders no editable text of
 * its own — it only READS layout.businessName / layout.tagline (the title),
 * content.description, layout.favicon and layout.ogImage. Every data-field,
 * data-image-field and data-href-field hook lives in a section component.
 * Section visibility is the 13 camelCase `visibility.*` keys below, every one
 * tested `!== false` (undefined means render).
 *
 * THE ONE HARDCODED VISIBLE STRING in the template is the skip link's
 * "Skip to content". It is an a11y affordance, visible on focus only. Flagged
 * here so it reads as a decision, not an oversight.
 *
 * PROP PLUMBING: every section is handed BOTH `content` and `layout`, even the
 * ones whose contract lists only content.* keys. Extra props are inert in
 * Astro, whereas a section reaching for layout.contact.phone with no `layout`
 * prop throws at build.
 *
 * DESIGN ISOLATION: every selector in the global block is prefixed
 * `html[data-page="BQ"]`, including the reset, body, img, a and ::selection, so
 * nothing leaks into a sister wrapper built in the same run — and nothing leaks
 * in. index.astro bundles all wrappers into ONE stylesheet; an unscoped rule
 * here would repaint every other template in the product.
 *
 * THEMING: the native palette is emitted FIRST and the engine's
 * `html:root{ ... !important}` block LAST in the head, which is the only reason
 * an explicit admin colour pick wins the cascade. Never move it above the
 * design's global style block or above the font link.
 *
 * FONT-PAIRING SENTINEL (two lines, wrapper-local): lib/astro-builder.ts
 * defaults `layout.fontPairing` to the literal 'modern', and resolveTheme's
 * `lockVariant` only blanks ''/'auto'/'default' — so without the sentinel
 * buildOverrideCss force-swaps Oswald + Source Sans with !important on nearly
 * every real site and the design never reaches a visitor. astro-builder's
 * DEFAULT is treated as unset; a deliberate admin pick still applies.
 *
 * FORBIDDEN CLASS NAMES in this template (read lib/genericThemeOverrides.ts
 * before adding a button anywhere):
 *   .btn-primary .btn-ghost .btn-yellow .btn-light .nav-cta .nav-right
 *   .testi .cta-band .trust, and `hero` as a class on a section element.
 * The engine pins those with !important for grounds this design does not have.
 * The proof strip is .proofstrip, the closing band is .closing and the opening
 * section is .masthead precisely so those pins cannot reach them. Buttons are
 * .btn--fill / .btn--line / .linkc (double dash), which dodge
 * `.btn-primary{color:<on-primary>!important}` — sub-AA in 6 of 13 schemes.
 *
 * PALETTE — THE DESIGN IS THE SPECIFICATION. Every value below is lifted from
 * the source design. One value is NOT the design's: the eyebrow colour on the
 * stone bands. The design used #A82D12 there, which measures 3.96:1 on
 * #C9C4B8 — below AA for text that small. It ships as --accent-deep #8C1F08
 * (5.21:1). That is the single deviation and it changes no layout.
 *
 * THE STONE IS NOT --paper-2. --paper-2 is the panel tint the override engine
 * remaps. #C9C4B8 is its own token, --stone, because it is a full-bleed band
 * GROUND carrying near-black type; if the engine remapped it, an admin colour
 * pick could turn it dark and strand every word on it. Same reasoning as
 * PageBJ's --green. --on-stone is fixed with it, as a pair.
 *
 * INVERTED BANDS: a section that wants the stone ground carries BOTH its own
 * name and `band-stone` (e.g. class="proofstrip band-stone"). That one class
 * flips the headings, body, eyebrow, hairlines and both button treatments in
 * this file; a section must not restate them.
 *
 * RENDER ORDER: Header, Hero, Trust, About, Services, Why, Gallery, How,
 * Testimonials, Credentials, Location, Area, Faq, CtaBand, Footer. The job
 * sheet sits high because on this vertical the question is always "can you
 * make this, out of what, and by when".
 *
 * Leaflet: this wrapper defines window.__tradesBQInitMap (variant-unique) and
 * LocationBQ calls that exact string. Keep `el.innerHTML = ''` in the boot — it
 * is what erases the drawn fallback plate — and keep id="map" literal.
 *
 * lockVariant: true — only an EXPLICIT admin colour/font pick recolours; the
 * hand-tuned palette wins by default.
 */
import HeaderBQ from './header/HeaderBQ.astro';
import HeroBQ from './hero/HeroBQ.astro';
import TrustBQ from './trust/TrustBQ.astro';
import AboutBQ from './about/AboutBQ.astro';
import ServicesBQ from './services/ServicesBQ.astro';
import WhyBQ from './why/WhyBQ.astro';
import GalleryBQ from './gallery/GalleryBQ.astro';
import HowBQ from './how/HowBQ.astro';
import TestimonialsBQ from './testimonials/TestimonialsBQ.astro';
import CredentialsBQ from './credentials/CredentialsBQ.astro';
import LocationBQ from './location/LocationBQ.astro';
import AreaBQ from './area/AreaBQ.astro';
import FaqBQ from './faq/FaqBQ.astro';
import CtaBandBQ from './ctaBand/CtaBandBQ.astro';
import FooterBQ from './footer/FooterBQ.astro';
import { resolveTheme, buildFontHref, buildOverrideCss } from '../../lib/genericThemeOverrides';

interface Props { siteData: any; }
const { siteData } = Astro.props;
const layout = siteData.layout ?? {};
const content = siteData.content ?? {};
const visibility = siteData.visibility ?? {};
const title = layout.businessName
  ? `${layout.businessName}${layout.tagline ? ' — ' + layout.tagline : ''}`
  : 'Welcome';
const { scheme: __themeScheme, pairing: __resolvedPairing } = resolveTheme(layout, (content as any).business_type, { lockVariant: true });
// 'modern' is astro-builder's DEFAULT, not a choice. Treating it as unset keeps
// Oswald + Source Sans 3; a deliberate admin pick still applies.
const __themePairing = __resolvedPairing === 'modern' ? '' : __resolvedPairing;
const __overrideCss = buildOverrideCss(__themeScheme, __themePairing);
const __fontHref = buildFontHref(__themePairing);
---

<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en" data-page="BQ">
<head>
  <meta charset="UTF-8" />
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0" />
  <title>{title}</title>
  {content.description && <meta name="description" content={content.description} />}
  <!-- Browser-chrome tint. A meta tag cannot read a CSS var, so this duplicates
       the sheet ground token (--paper). -->
  <meta name="theme-color" content="#111213" />
  <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com" />
  <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.gstatic.com" crossorigin="" />
  <!-- Native fonts, taken verbatim from the design. Oswald carries every
       heading, label and figure; Source Sans 3 carries body copy. Always loaded
       so the variant reads as designed even when the admin never touched the
       font dropdown. -->
  <link href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Oswald:wght@400;500;600;700&family=Source+Sans+3:wght@400;600;700&display=swap" rel="stylesheet" />
  <link rel="stylesheet" href="https://unpkg.com/leaflet@1.9.4/dist/leaflet.css" integrity="sha256-p4NxAoJBhIIN+hmNHrzRCf9tD/miZyoHS5obTRR9BMY=" crossorigin="" />
  {layout.favicon && <link rel="icon" href={layout.favicon} />}
  {(layout.ogImage || layout.favicon) && <meta property="og:image" content={layout.ogImage || layout.favicon} />}

  <style is:global>
    /* ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
       PageBQ · "Bakal Fabrication Works" — trades (steel fabrication, welding).
       Tokens + shared base primitives. EVERY selector is prefixed
       html[data-page="BQ"] so nothing leaks into a sister wrapper, or in.

       FIVE LOAD-BEARING FACTS. Do not tidy any of them:

       1. SPECIFICITY. Every appearance-bearing base primitive is wrapped in
          :where() -> (0,1,1), so an Astro-scoped single-compound section rule
          (0,2,0) wins. Removing a :where() is the documented cause of every
          photo frame in a template collapsing to the base height. BELT AND
          BRACES: sections also size .plate with an INLINE
          style="aspect-ratio:X" — inline outranks every selector, so the
          specificity argument never has to be won twice.

       2. BUTTON CLASS NAMES. .btn--fill / .btn--line / .linkc, double dash, on
          purpose. NEVER use in this template: .btn-primary .btn-ghost
          .btn-yellow .btn-light .nav-cta .nav-right .testi .cta-band .trust,
          or class="hero" on a section. See the FORBIDDEN list in the
          frontmatter for what each engine pin would break here.

       3. HOVER NEVER GOES TRANSPARENT AND NEVER CHANGES HUE. An inset
          rgba(0,0,0,.18) darkens the fill and paints below the label, so a
          label can never strand mid-transition. That is the exact trap that
          has stranded button labels in this product before.

       4. FOCUS. One DUO ring everywhere: a 3px var(--paper) outline inside a
          6px var(--ink) halo. Built from the ink/paper pair, so it separates on
          the sheet, on the stone band and on the orange band alike.

       5. HEAD ORDER. This block must be followed by the font link and then, as
          the LAST node in the head, a global style node fed the override CSS.
          The engine's html:root{ ... !important} only beats these tokens
          because it comes later in source order. (Never write a literal closing
          style or script tag inside this block, comments included — it is a
          raw-text element, so the parser would end the stylesheet right there.)
    ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ */

    html[data-page="BQ"] {
      /* GROUNDS. --paper is the BACKGROUND (the near-black sheet) and --ink is
         the text on it. The design named its light value "paper"; the generic
         alias contract this product shares needs --paper to mean the ground, so
         the two are swapped here and every component reads var(--ink) where the
         design read its light token. Do not re-swap them. */
      --paper: #111213;
      --paper-2: #1D1F22;
      --paper-3: #0A0B0C;
      --card: #1D1F22;
      --ink: #ECEAE4;
      --ink-soft: #C9C4B8;
      --muted: #8A867C;
      --line: #33353A;
      /* THE HAZARD ORANGE-RED. Ink on it measures 4.91:1. */
      --accent: #F0421F;
      --accent-deep: #8C1F08;
      /* THE STONE. Its own token, never --paper-2: it is a full-bleed band
         GROUND carrying near-black type. If the engine remapped it, an admin
         colour pick could turn it dark and strand every word on it. */
      --stone: #C9C4B8;
      --on-stone: #111213;
      --on-stone-soft: #4A4A48;
      --stone-line: rgba(17,18,19,.18);
      /* rgb triplets for token-driven tints */
      --paper-rgb: 17,18,19;
      --ink-rgb: 236,234,228;
      --accent-rgb: 240,66,31;
      --stone-rgb: 201,196,184;
      /* contrast aliases the override engine and inherited rules expect */
      --on-ink: #111213;
      --on-paper: #ECEAE4;
      --on-accent: #111213;
      --on-primary: #111213;
      /* type + metrics */
      --disp: "Oswald", "Arial Narrow", Impact, system-ui, sans-serif;
      --display: "Oswald", "Arial Narrow", Impact, system-ui, sans-serif;
      --cond: "Oswald", "Arial Narrow", Impact, system-ui, sans-serif;
      --sans: "Source Sans 3", system-ui, -apple-system, "Segoe UI", Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif;
      --body: "Source Sans 3", system-ui, -apple-system, "Segoe UI", Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif;
      /* This design has no monospace and no serif: its small tracked caps are
         Oswald. Both tokens exist because the engine sets them and shared
         primitives read them. */
      --mono: "Oswald", "Arial Narrow", Impact, system-ui, sans-serif;
      --serif: "Source Sans 3", system-ui, -apple-system, Georgia, serif;
      --maxw: 1280px;
      --pad: clamp(16px, 4vw, 44px);
    }

    /* VERIFIED CONTRAST (sRGB relative luminance, the design's palette):
       ink/paper 15.6 · ink-soft/paper 10.8 · muted/paper 5.16
       on-stone/stone 10.8 · on-stone-soft/stone 5.10 · accent-deep/stone 5.21
       on-accent/accent 4.91
       accent/paper 3.18 — LARGE display figures and 11-12px tracked eyebrows
       only, never body copy. Every eyebrow in this template is followed by a
       heading that repeats its meaning, so a dimmed eyebrow degrades rather
       than breaks.
       THE ONE DEVIATION from the design: its #A82D12 eyebrow on stone measured
       3.96:1 and ships as --accent-deep #8C1F08 at 5.21:1. */

    /* ── reset + document ─────────────────────────────────────────────── */
    html[data-page="BQ"] *,
    html[data-page="BQ"] *::before,
    html[data-page="BQ"] *::after { box-sizing: border-box; }
    html[data-page="BQ"] {
      -webkit-text-size-adjust: 100%; scroll-behavior: smooth;
      /* The header is sticky and ~62px tall; every in-page anchor landed with
         the top of its target underneath it. scroll-padding-top on the root
         beats per-section scroll-margin-top: one declaration, it covers nested
         targets, and it keeps keyboard focus out from under the bar too. */
      scroll-padding-top: 86px;
    }
    @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) { html[data-page="BQ"] { scroll-behavior: auto; } }
    html[data-page="BQ"] body {
      margin: 0; padding: 0;
      background-color: var(--paper); color: var(--ink);
      font-family: var(--sans); font-size: 17px; line-height: 1.62;
      -webkit-font-smoothing: antialiased; overflow-x: hidden;
    }
    html[data-page="BQ"] img { max-width: 100%; display: block; }
    html[data-page="BQ"] a { color: inherit; text-decoration: none; }
    html[data-page="BQ"] ::selection { background: var(--accent); color: var(--on-accent); }
    /* text-transform is DECLARED, not defaulted. Two templates once shipped an
       unscoped h1,h2,h3,h4{text-transform:uppercase} in an is:global block and,
       because index.astro bundles every wrapper's globals into one stylesheet,
       it capitalised unrelated designs. Uppercase is this design's signature,
       so it is set here — on scoped selectors only. */
    html[data-page="BQ"] :where(h1,h2,h3,h4) {
      margin: 0; font-family: var(--disp); font-weight: 700;
      line-height: .95; letter-spacing: -.005em; text-transform: uppercase;
      color: var(--ink);
    }
    /* This bare-element paragraph reset is (0,1,1): always qualify a section's
       own paragraph rules with a parent class so they win. */
    html[data-page="BQ"] :where(p) { margin: 0 0 1em; }

    /* ── layout scaffolding ───────────────────────────────────────────── */
    html[data-page="BQ"] :where(.wrap) { width: min(var(--maxw), 100%); margin-inline: auto; padding-inline: var(--pad); }
    html[data-page="BQ"] section { position: relative; }
    html[data-page="BQ"] :where(.sec) { padding-block: clamp(46px, 7vw, 76px); border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line); }

    /* ── THE STONE BAND. One class, applied alongside a section's own name. It
          flips headings, body, eyebrows, hairlines and BOTH button variants, so
          no section restates any of them. */
    html[data-page="BQ"] :where(.band-stone) { background-color: var(--stone); color: var(--on-stone); border-bottom-color: var(--stone-line); }
    html[data-page="BQ"] :where(.band-stone) :where(h1,h2,h3,h4) { color: var(--on-stone); }
    html[data-page="BQ"] :where(.band-stone) .kick { color: var(--accent-deep); }
    html[data-page="BQ"] :where(.band-stone) .lede,
    html[data-page="BQ"] :where(.band-stone) .body,
    html[data-page="BQ"] :where(.band-stone) .label { color: var(--on-stone-soft); }
    html[data-page="BQ"] :where(.band-stone) .rowrule { border-bottom-color: var(--stone-line); }

    /* ── .kick — the eyebrow. Tracked Oswald caps in the hazard orange. */
    html[data-page="BQ"] :where(.kick) {
      display: inline-block;
      font-family: var(--disp); font-weight: 500; font-size: 12px;
      letter-spacing: .28em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--accent);
    }
    /* ── .label — the quiet tracked caps every ledger key and chip uses. */
    html[data-page="BQ"] :where(.label) {
      font-family: var(--disp); font-weight: 400; font-size: 11px;
      letter-spacing: .16em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--muted);
    }
    /* ── .h2 — the section headline. Uppercase condensed, tight leading. */
    html[data-page="BQ"] :where(.h2) {
      font-family: var(--disp); font-weight: 600;
      font-size: clamp(30px, 4.2vw, 56px); line-height: .98;
      text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: -.005em; margin: 0;
    }
    html[data-page="BQ"] :where(.lede) { color: var(--ink-soft); font-size: clamp(15.5px, 1.5vw, 18px); line-height: 1.66; margin: 0; }
    html[data-page="BQ"] :where(.body) { color: var(--ink-soft); font-size: 15.5px; line-height: 1.72; margin: 0; }
    /* ── .fig — the oversized figure (trust cells, why numerals, step numbers). */
    html[data-page="BQ"] :where(.fig) {
      font-family: var(--disp); font-weight: 700; line-height: .85;
      font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums lining-nums;
    }

    /* ── .sec-head — eyebrow over headline, used by most sections. */
    html[data-page="BQ"] :where(.sec-head) { display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 10px; margin-bottom: clamp(26px, 3.4vw, 40px); }

    /* ── BUTTONS ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────
       .btn--fill  the hazard fill, ink label (4.91:1)
       .btn--line  hairline outline, ink-coloured label
       On the stone band both invert, declared once here so no section is
       tempted to restate them and drift. */
    html[data-page="BQ"] :where(.btn) {
      /* DECLARED, not left to chance. index.astro bundles every template's
         is:global CSS onto every page, so an unscoped `.btn{background: ...}`
         from another family has painted outline controls elsewhere before. */
      background-color: transparent;
      display: inline-flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; gap: .5em;
      padding: 15px 26px; min-height: 48px;
      border: 1px solid transparent;
      font-family: var(--disp); font-weight: 500; font-size: 12px;
      letter-spacing: .16em; text-transform: uppercase; text-decoration: none;
      cursor: pointer; white-space: nowrap;
      transition: background-color .18s ease, box-shadow .18s ease, transform .18s ease, border-color .18s ease, color .18s ease;
    }
    html[data-page="BQ"] :where(.btn--fill) { background-color: var(--accent); color: var(--on-accent); border-color: var(--accent); }
    html[data-page="BQ"] :where(.btn--fill:hover) {
      background-color: var(--accent); color: var(--on-accent); border-color: var(--accent);
      box-shadow: inset 0 0 0 999px rgba(0,0,0,.18); transform: translateY(-2px);
    }
    html[data-page="BQ"] :where(.btn--fill:active) { transform: translateY(0); }
    html[data-page="BQ"] :where(.btn--line) { background-color: transparent; color: var(--ink); border-color: var(--ink-soft); }
    html[data-page="BQ"] :where(.btn--line:hover) {
      background-color: var(--ink); color: var(--on-ink); border-color: var(--ink); transform: translateY(-2px);
    }
    html[data-page="BQ"] :where(.btn--line:active) { transform: translateY(0); }
    /* On the stone band both flip to near-black on stone. */
    html[data-page="BQ"] :where(.band-stone) .btn--line { color: var(--on-stone); border-color: var(--on-stone); }
    html[data-page="BQ"] :where(.band-stone) .btn--line:hover { background-color: var(--on-stone); color: var(--stone); border-color: var(--on-stone); }
    html[data-page="BQ"] :where(.band-stone) .btn--fill { background-color: var(--on-stone); color: var(--stone); border-color: var(--on-stone); }
    html[data-page="BQ"] :where(.band-stone) .btn--fill:hover { background-color: var(--on-stone); color: var(--stone); border-color: var(--on-stone); box-shadow: inset 0 0 0 999px rgba(255,255,255,.12); }
    @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
      html[data-page="BQ"] .btn { transition: none; }
      html[data-page="BQ"] .btn--fill:hover, html[data-page="BQ"] .btn--line:hover { transform: none; }
    }

    /* ── .linkc — quiet text-link action, carries no .btn class so the engine's
          label pins cannot reach it. Its colour never changes on hover (only
          the rule under it thickens), so it cannot fail a contrast check
          mid-interaction. */
    html[data-page="BQ"] :where(.linkc) {
      display: inline-flex; align-items: center; gap: .5em; min-height: 44px;
      font-family: var(--disp); font-weight: 500; font-size: 12px;
      letter-spacing: .16em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--accent);
      border-bottom: 2px solid var(--accent); padding-bottom: 2px;
      transition: border-bottom-width .18s ease, transform .18s ease;
    }
    html[data-page="BQ"] :where(.linkc:hover) { color: var(--accent); border-bottom-width: 3px; transform: translateY(-1px); }
    html[data-page="BQ"] :where(.band-stone) .linkc { color: var(--accent-deep); border-bottom-color: var(--accent-deep); }
    @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) { html[data-page="BQ"] .linkc { transition: none; } }

    /* ── FOCUS · the DUO ring. See load-bearing fact 4. */
    html[data-page="BQ"] :where(a,button,summary,[tabindex]):focus-visible {
      outline: 3px solid var(--paper); outline-offset: 0; box-shadow: 0 0 0 6px var(--ink);
    }

    /* ── .plate — THE photo frame. Every image in the template is one of these.
          Sections size it with an inline style="aspect-ratio:X". The fallback
          face is token-built, so it recolours with the scheme — and a section
          must OMIT the plate entirely when the owner supplied no photo rather
          than ship a decorative empty box. */
    html[data-page="BQ"] :where(.plate) {
      position: relative; overflow: hidden; isolation: isolate;
      background-color: var(--paper-2); border: 1px solid var(--line);
    }
    html[data-page="BQ"] :where(.plate) .ph {
      position: absolute; inset: 0; z-index: 1;
      background-color: var(--paper-2);
      background-size: cover; background-position: center; background-repeat: no-repeat;
      background-image:
        linear-gradient(140deg, rgba(var(--accent-rgb),.20), transparent 58%),
        repeating-linear-gradient(0deg, rgba(var(--ink-rgb),.06) 0 1px, transparent 1px 22px),
        repeating-linear-gradient(90deg, rgba(var(--ink-rgb),.06) 0 1px, transparent 1px 22px);
      transition: transform .5s ease;
    }
    /* .cap — caption on an OPAQUE bar, never a gradient scrim: legible over ANY
       owner photo, however dark or blown out. */
    html[data-page="BQ"] :where(.plate) .cap {
      position: absolute; left: 0; bottom: 0; z-index: 3; max-width: 100%;
      background-color: var(--paper); color: var(--ink-soft);
      font-family: var(--disp); font-weight: 400; font-size: 11px;
      letter-spacing: .16em; text-transform: uppercase; padding: 7px 12px;
    }
    html[data-page="BQ"] :where(.plate) .cap.on { background-color: var(--accent); color: var(--on-accent); }
    @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) { html[data-page="BQ"] :where(.plate) .ph { transition: none; } }

    /* ── .rowrule — the one hairline row separator every ledger in the template
          uses (spec table, job sheet, hours, FAQ). Per-cell border, never a
          gap-over-inked-container trick: that paints a visible block in the
          EMPTY tracks of a partial last row. */
    html[data-page="BQ"] :where(.rowrule) { border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line); }

    /* ── scroll reveal (the boot at the end of the body toggles .in) ── */
    html[data-page="BQ"] :where(.reveal) { opacity: 0; transform: translateY(18px); transition: opacity .7s ease, transform .7s ease; }
    html[data-page="BQ"] :where(.reveal.in) { opacity: 1; transform: none; }
    @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
      html[data-page="BQ"] .reveal { opacity: 1 !important; transform: none !important; transition: none !important; }
    }

    /* ── skip link ────────────────────────────────────────────────────── */
    html[data-page="BQ"] :where(.skip) {
      position: absolute; left: -999px; top: 0; z-index: 100;
      background-color: var(--accent); color: var(--on-accent); padding: 12px 18px;
      font-family: var(--disp); font-weight: 500; font-size: 12px;
      letter-spacing: .16em; text-transform: uppercase;
    }
    html[data-page="BQ"] :where(.skip:focus) { left: 0; top: 0; }

    /* ── SHARED MOBILE PASS · 760px ───────────────────────────────────── */
    @media (max-width: 760px) {
      html[data-page="BQ"] :where(.sec) { padding-block: clamp(38px, 9vw, 56px); }
      /* The MAX is the BASE clamp's own value at 760px (31.9px), not a round
         number. Anything higher and the headline GROWS as the viewport narrows
         past 761 — a jump no screenshot at 1440 or 375 can show you. */
      html[data-page="BQ"] :where(.h2) { font-size: clamp(26px, 7vw, 32px); overflow-wrap: anywhere; }
      html[data-page="BQ"] :where(.lede) { max-width: none; }
    }
    /* ── SHARED MOBILE PASS · 520px (verified no horizontal overflow at 360px) ── */
    @media (max-width: 520px) {
      html[data-page="BQ"] body { font-size: 16px; }
      html[data-page="BQ"] :where(.h2) { font-size: clamp(23px, 8vw, 30px); }
      html[data-page="BQ"] :where(.kick) { font-size: 11px; letter-spacing: .2em; }
      html[data-page="BQ"] :where(.btn) { padding: 14px 20px; white-space: normal; text-align: center; flex: 1 1 100%; }
    }
  </style>

  {__fontHref && <link href={__fontHref} rel="stylesheet" />}
  <style is:global set:html={__overrideCss}></style>
</head>
<body>
  <a class="skip" href="#main">Skip to content</a>
  <HeaderBQ layout={layout} content={content} />
  <main id="main">
    {visibility.heroSection !== false && <HeroBQ content={content} layout={layout} />}
    {visibility.trustBlock !== false && <TrustBQ content={content} layout={layout} />}
    {visibility.aboutSection !== false && <AboutBQ content={content} layout={layout} />}
    {visibility.servicesSection !== false && <ServicesBQ content={content} layout={layout} />}
    {visibility.whyUsBlock !== false && <WhyBQ content={content} layout={layout} />}
    {visibility.gallerySection !== false && <GalleryBQ content={content} layout={layout} />}
    {visibility.howItWorksBlock !== false && <HowBQ content={content} layout={layout} />}
    {visibility.testimonialsBlock !== false && <TestimonialsBQ content={content} layout={layout} />}
    {visibility.credentialsBlock !== false && <CredentialsBQ content={content} layout={layout} />}
    {visibility.locationBlock !== false && <LocationBQ content={content} layout={layout} />}
    {visibility.serviceAreaBlock !== false && <AreaBQ content={content} layout={layout} />}
    {visibility.faqBlock !== false && <FaqBQ content={content} layout={layout} />}
  </main>
  {visibility.ctaBandBlock !== false && <CtaBandBQ content={content} layout={layout} />}
  <FooterBQ layout={layout} content={content} />

  <script is:inline src="https://unpkg.com/leaflet@1.9.4/dist/leaflet.js" integrity="sha256-20nQCchB9co0qIjJZRGuk2/Z9VM+kNiyxNV1lvTlZBo=" crossorigin=""></script>
  <script is:inline>
    (function () {
      var reduce = window.matchMedia('(prefers-reduced-motion: reduce)').matches;
      if (!reduce && !document.hidden) {
        var io = new IntersectionObserver(function (es) {
          es.forEach(function (e) { if (e.isIntersecting) { e.target.classList.add('in'); io.unobserve(e.target); } });
        }, { threshold: 0.1, rootMargin: '0px 0px -8% 0px' });
        document.querySelectorAll('.reveal').forEach(function (el) { io.observe(el); });
      } else {
        document.querySelectorAll('.reveal').forEach(function (el) { el.classList.add('in'); });
      }
      // Bakal / BQ Leaflet boot — accepts (lat, lng, label) from LocationBQ. The
      // global name is variant-unique on purpose: a preview harness can render
      // two wrappers in one document, and a shared name cross-wires the maps.
      window.__tradesBQInitMap = function (lat, lng, label) {
        if (!window.L) return;
        var el = document.getElementById('map'); if (!el) return;
        // Erases LocationBQ's drawn fallback plate; without this the tiles stack
        // on top of the drawn grid.
        el.innerHTML = '';
        var map = L.map('map', { scrollWheelZoom: false }).setView([lat, lng], 15);
        // LABELLED basemap: a customer driving a truck to a yard needs road and
        // barangay names.
        L.tileLayer('https://basemaps.cartocdn.com/rastertiles/dark_all/{z}/{x}/{y}{r}.png', { attribution: '&copy; OpenStreetMap &copy; CARTO', maxZoom: 19, subdomains: 'abcd' }).addTo(map);
        // Marker colours are READ from the live tokens rather than baked, so an
        // explicit admin colour pick recolours the pin too.
        var cs = window.getComputedStyle(document.documentElement);
        var accent = (cs.getPropertyValue('--accent') || '').trim() || '#F0421F';
        var paper = (cs.getPropertyValue('--paper') || '').trim() || '#111213';
        var icon = L.divIcon({
          className: '',
          html: '<div style="width:16px;height:16px;background:' + accent + ';box-shadow:0 0 0 3px ' + paper + ';"></div>',
          iconSize: [16, 16], iconAnchor: [8, 8],
        });
        L.marker([lat, lng], { icon: icon }).addTo(map).bindPopup('<b>' + label + '</b>');
      };
    })();
  </script>
</body>
</html>
